# frozen from the reference: zeroconf 0.151.3, CPython 3.12.15
# regenerate: env -u PYTHONPATH .venv/bin/python \
#   scripts/mdns_announce_probe.py --protocol cast --fixture --dump-hex <this file>
# inputs: service=_googlecast._tcp.local. instance=Macast-Fixture-1._googlecast._tcp.local. server=Macast-Fixture-1.local. port=8009 address=192.0.2.7
# txt (order as written on the wire): id=00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007;fn=Macast(Fixture-1.local);ca=5;st=0;bs=FA8B;ic=/setup/icon.png;ve=05;md=Macast;rm=Macast;rs=Macast Receiver
#
# TWO announce lines, not one, because the reference does not have an
# order for that pair. `_get_address_and_nsec_records` returns a `set`, and
# measured on this build: PYTHONHASHSEED 0/1/2 emit `NSEC, A` while
# PYTHONHASHSEED 12345 emits `A, NSEC`. So a writer that matches either one
# is faithful, and a corpus that pinned one would be pinning a hash seed.
# PTR, SRV and TXT *are* a fixed order (added explicitly in
# `_add_broadcast_answer`), and they are byte-identical in all four lines.
announce-nsec-first 
announce-a-first 
goodbye-nsec-first 
goodbye-a-first 
probe 0000040000010000000100000b5f676f6f676c6563617374045f746370056c6f63616c00000c8001c00c000c0001000011940013104d61636173742d466978747572652d31c00c
